      "message": "fix(rotary): judge a subplate from where it stands; a stated nose_to_axis never loosens the swing check\n\nReview fixes on PR #1082 (NeoTech's review of 642cd694):\n- rotary_stack: each subplate's posed top over the machine table's top\n  is read beside its linked stack and the larger wins (a gap above the\n  links is a named layer); no table or no posed geometry refuses by name.\n  A subplate put on a plate by position, or left up after its plate was\n  deleted, is no longer judged on its own 19.05 mm.\n- check_stated: a stated nose_to_axis above the machine's own figure, or\n  above the machine's less the setup's own stack, is refused by name at\n  the gate - also after a datum transfer onto a taller stack.\n- Machine page: \"spindle nose to rotary centerline\", not the file key;\n  the stated-figure refusal shows beside the field.\n\nPinned by rotary_subplate_standing (5 tests); rotary_subplate,\nmcp_rotary_stack and ui setup_rotary fixtures stand on the table.\n\nRefs #821\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
